WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.376
Object detection identifies configured categories and their locations in a frame.

00:00:04.376 --> 00:00:08.652
Image classification assigns a label to an image or cropped region.

00:00:08.652 --> 00:00:10.596
Scene-description models generate natural-language summaries,

00:00:10.596 --> 00:00:15.260
while activity-recognition systems examine change across time rather than a single picture.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:19.148
Vision-language models can answer broader questions about images or clips.

00:00:19.148 --> 00:00:24.590
Their flexibility is useful for review and summarization, but output can vary with wording,

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.145
model version, and context.

00:00:26.145 --> 00:00:29.643
A fluent description is not necessarily a correct one.

00:00:29.643 --> 00:00:35.863
A false positive occurs when the system reports an event that did not happen as described.

00:00:35.863 --> 00:00:39.750
A false negative occurs when a relevant event is missed.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.471
Both matter: excessive false alerts create fatigue,

00:00:42.471 --> 00:00:44.804
while missed events create misplaced confidence.

00:00:44.804 --> 00:00:48.691
Lighting, weather, shadows, camera angle, distance, occlusion, dirty lenses, compression,

00:00:48.691 --> 00:00:51.801
frame rate, and motion blur can change results.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:56.465
Models also face domain shift when the local scene differs from their

00:00:56.465 --> 00:00:58.798
training data or changes over time.

00:00:58.798 --> 00:01:02.296
Confidence values are model-specific signals, not guarantees of truth.

00:01:02.296 --> 00:01:04.629
Thresholds trade sensitivity against false alerts.

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:08.516
Evaluate performance with representative local footage, including daytime, night, seasons,

00:01:08.516 --> 00:01:11.237
common objects, and unusual but legitimate activity.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:16.291
Treat AI output as assistance, not proof of identity, intent, wrongdoing, or safety.

00:01:16.291 --> 00:01:19.400
Preserve context for authorized human review, document limitations,

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.344
and avoid high-consequence automatic action.

00:01:21.344 --> 00:01:25.620
Responsible use begins by admitting what the model cannot reliably know.
